            <ArticleTitle>Gut microbiota: Ganoderma lucidum, a new prebiotic agent to treat obesity?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>553-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/nrgastro.2015.137</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Modulation of the gut microbiota is one of the promising tools to tackle obesity. Chang and colleagues have recently shown that an extract of the mushroom Ganoderma lucidum, a traditional remedy in Asia, can reduce obesity in mice by modulating the gut microbiota, thereby exerting a prebiotic effect.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
